  "items": [
    {
      "detail": "0x001 · U-mode",
      "documentation": "CSR · Floating-Point Accrued Exceptions · 0x001 · U-mode\n\n```riscv\nfflags\n```\n\n---\n\nFields:\n- `NV` [4] — Set by hardware when a floating point operation is invalid and stays set until explicitly cleared by software.\n- `DZ` [3] — Set by hardware when a floating point divide attempts to divide by zero and stays set until explicitly cleared by software.\n- `OF` [2] — Set by hardware when a floating point operation overflows and stays set until explicitly cleared by software.\n- `UF` [1] — Set by hardware when a floating point operation underflows and stays set until explicitly cleared by software.\n- `NX` [0] — Set by hardware when a floating point operation is inexact and stays set until explicitly cleared by software.\n\n---\n\nThe accrued exception flags indicate the exception conditions that have arisen on any floating-point arithmetic instruction since the field was last reset by software.",
      "insertText": "fflags",
      "kind": 21,
      "label": "fflags"
    },
    {
      "detail": "0x002 · U-mode",
      "documentation": "CSR · Floating-Point Dynamic Rounding Mode · 0x002 · U-mode\n\n```riscv\nfrm\n```\n\n---\n\nFields:\n- `ROUNDINGMODE` [2:0] — Rounding mode data.\n\n---\n\nThe behavior of floating-point instructions that depend on rounding mode when executed with a reserved rounding mode is _reserved_, including both static reserved rounding modes (101-110) and dynamic reserved rounding modes (101-111).",
      "insertText": "frm",
      "kind": 21,
      "label": "frm"
    },
    {
      "detail": "0x003 · U-mode",
      "documentation": "CSR · Floating-point control and status register (`frm` + `fflags`) · 0x003 · U-mode\n\n```riscv\nfcsr\n```\n\n---\n\nFields:\n- `FRM` [7:5] — A value of 111 in the instruction's _rm_ field selects the dynamic rounding mode held in `frm`.\n- `NV` [4] — Invalid Operation.\n- `DZ` [3] — Divide by zero.\n- `OF` [2] — Overflow.\n- `UF` [1] — Underflow.\n- `NX` [0] — Inexact.\n\n---\n\nThe floating-point control and status register, `fcsr`, is a RISC-V control and status register (CSR).",
      "insertText": "fcsr",
      "kind": 21,
      "label": "fcsr"
    },
    {
      "detail": "0x008 · U-mode",
      "documentation": "CSR · Vector Start Index · 0x008 · U-mode\n\n```riscv\nvstart\n```\n\n---\n\nFields:\n- `VALUE` [63:0] — Normally, vstart is only written by hardware on a trap on a vector instruction, with the vstart value representing the element on which…\n\n---\n\nSpecifies the index of the first element to be executed by a vector instruction.",
      "insertText": "vstart",
      "kind": 21,
      "label": "vstart"
    },
    {
      "detail": "0x009 · U-mode",
      "documentation": "CSR · Vector Fixed-Point Saturate Flag · 0x009 · U-mode\n\n```riscv\nvxsat\n```\n\n---\n\nFields:\n- `VALUE` [63:0] — The vxsat CSR has a single read-write least-significant bit (vxsat[0]) that indicates if a fixed-point instruction has had to saturate an…\n\n---\n\nIndicates if a fixed-point instruction has had to saturate an output value to fit into a destination format.",
      "insertText": "vxsat",
      "kind": 21,
      "label": "vxsat"
    },
